ion on hand to Jena Nelson's $84,000, and has highlighted federal community project funding for the district. Nearly every professional rating places the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, though a few outlets call it Likely R.\n\nDemocrats see a rare opening in Oklahoma: Nelson won her primary, national party groups have signaled investment, and a Democratic-sponsored September poll showed her trailing by five points. Still, that poll is the only public survey, it came from a Democratic-leaning sponsor, and prediction markets price Nelson's chances at about one in ten. The evidence supports a Republican win in the high single digits, with meaningful but limited uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0816, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0827, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0449, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0713, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0529, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0783, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.059, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem"